        {
          "name": "3d6 Roll-Under Check",
          "expression": "3d6",
          "resultMode": "band",
          "description": "Roll 3d6 against a skill or attribute — success on a result at or under it. Fired from a field's own roll button, which passes that field's current value as the target. A natural 3 or 4 is always a Critical Success; a natural 18 is always a Critical Failure; a natural 17 is a Critical Failure unless the skill/attribute is 16 or higher (in which case it's still a plain Failure — a 17 never succeeds outright). Two real GURPS refinements aren't modeled here: a natural 5 or 6 is ALSO a Critical Success if the skill is 15+/16+ respectively, and failing by 10 or more is ALSO a Critical Failure regardless of the roll — both require comparing against the skill by a margin the current band engine doesn't express (targetMaxFraction compares to a FRACTION of the target, not a fixed offset from it), so they're flagged here rather than silently misrepresented.",
          "bands": [
            {
              "max": 4,
              "label": "Critical Success"
            },
            {
              "min": 18,
              "label": "Critical Failure"
            },
